1
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,940
=When the Lights Rise=
=Episode 4=

2
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:14,700
I've heard the ladies mention

3
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:17,100
a kind of wine that's extremely potent
and takes effect quickly,

4
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:18,700
sold only to men.

5
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,100
Could that be coca wine?

6
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,300
That's right.

7
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:25,060
It's also called Night of Passion
or Golden Dreams.

8
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:26,300
After looking into it,

9
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:28,460
I found quite a few
dance halls selling it.

10
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:31,700
But

11
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:33,700
with the New Life Movement
cracking down so hard,

12
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:35,260
how dare they be so brazen?

13
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,500
Of course they wouldn't dare openly.

14
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:38,220
These are all prohibited goods,

15
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:39,100
smuggled in illegally.

16
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,660
The Kuang family is behind the supply.

17
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:42,420
The Kuang family?

18
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,700
Why would they get involved
in such shady business?

19
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:49,500
In Shanghai these days,

20
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:51,020
anything that makes money

21
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,860
is considered a good
business opportunity.

22
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:58,060
Are your informants reliable?

23
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:00,420
Will they really deliver
the goods here today?

24
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:01,180
They're reliable.

25
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,420
As long as their debts are waived,

26
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:05,300
they'll tell us everything they know.

27
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,100
Here they come.

28
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:15,020
Give me half an hour.

29
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,500
If I'm not out by then,

30
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,420
leave without me.

31
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:29,500
Miss Mei, long time no see.

32
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:30,900
Young Master Kuang.

33
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,220
What are you doing here?

34
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:36,180
There's been some trouble
at home lately.

35
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:37,220
I've been feeling troubled,

36
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:39,020
so I came out to unwind.

37
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,300
Don't leave.

38
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:42,500
Just finish this dance with me.

39
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,700
I came with a friend.

40
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:45,500
I need to find him.

41
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,060
You mean that loan shark?

42
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:49,220
I saw him heading toward the back.

43
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,020
Maybe he couldn't afford the bill

44
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,500
and slipped away.

45
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:55,340
Miss Mei.

46
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,460
Men simply can't be trusted.

47
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:00,700
Aren't you a man too?

48
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:02,060
I'm different from them.

49
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:03,460
How so?

50
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:04,820
You'll find out someday.

51
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:08,900
I have something to do. I must go.

52
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:11,660
Then shouldn't we talk about

53
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,020
your sister killing my father?

54
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,260
We still need to investigate

55
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:18,660
what really happened.

56
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:20,220
Investigating?

57
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:21,380
Who's investigating?

58
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:22,500
You?

59
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:24,620
What have you found out, Miss Mei?

60
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:28,300
Have a drink with me,

61
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:30,500
and I'll tell you a few things

62
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,260
about Mei Xiaozhu.

63
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:41,100
Young Master,
what would you like to drink today?

64
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:43,460
Miss Mei doesn't come to Kaimeili often.

65
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,420
Why don't I order for you?

66
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:57,700
Tell me what you know.

67
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:58,700
Quite a lot.

68
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,900
She was a regular at Kaimeili.

69
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,460
She dressed fashionably

70
00:06:02,460 --> 00:06:03,460
and had quite a fiery temper.

71
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:05,220
Compared to those ordinary girls,

72
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:07,020
she was much more interesting.

73
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:08,060
Are you saying

74
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:10,060
she came here often?

75
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:11,100
Of course.

76
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:12,660
She was very popular.

77
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:14,460
If you don't believe me,

78
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:18,020
go ask them.

79
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:19,420
Everyone here

80
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,420
remembers her very well.

81
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:23,260
What did you do to her?

82
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,180
We wouldn't dare do anything.

83
00:06:26,100 --> 00:06:27,460
She wouldn't even pay attention to

84
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:29,300
young men like us
who live off our families.

85
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:31,060
The men she liked

86
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:34,660
were successful men like my father.

87
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:35,540
Nonsense!

88
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,660
Why would I make that up?

89
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,300
But we do share the same taste.

90
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:41,020
I also dislike those young women

91
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,260
who only ask their families for money

92
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:43,700
and spend their days having fun.

93
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:47,180
Modern, independent women like you

94
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:48,900
are exactly my type.

95
00:06:50,850 --> 00:06:51,900
Leaving already?

96
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:53,500
I guess you really don't want to know

97
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,220
how your sister actually died.

98
00:06:58,340 --> 00:06:59,620
What exactly are you trying to say?

99
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:02,700
Not just anyone

100
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:04,900
can attend Mintong Middle School.

101
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:43,020
Coca leaves.

102
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:45,460
Coca wine.

103
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:42,260
Mei Xiaozhu and Ding Yiyi

104
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:45,100
were the only two ordinary
students admitted on scholarships.

105
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:48,580
Ding Yiyi.

106
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:51,620
You see,

107
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:52,860
once people get a taste

108
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:54,380
of things beyond their social class,

109
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:56,700
they inevitably start wanting them,

110
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,700
longing to possess them,

111
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:01,300
and eventually go astray.

112
00:09:03,180 --> 00:09:03,980
What do you mean?

113
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:06,460
I'm just reminding you.

114
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:08,220
Two ordinary students.

115
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,100
One is dead,

116
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:12,220
but the other is still alive.

117
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:15,660
Young Master, your drink.

118
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:17,580
Miss Mei.

119
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:19,900
I've told you everything I know.

120
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:21,700
Now,

121
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:24,220
you have to have this drink with me.

122
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:28,060
Whether I can believe you

123
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,300
is another matter.

124
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:31,300
Are you going back
on your word, Miss Mei?

125
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:36,100
Fine.

126
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:43,180
Miss Mei.

127
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:44,500
Miss Mei!

128
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:46,220
Miss Mei!

129
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:47,620
What's wrong?

130
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:48,300
Miss Mei.

131
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:51,020
Miss Mei, are you all right?

132
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:53,300
What did you give her to drink?

133
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:55,220
Do you know what kind of wine this is?

134
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:56,220
It's coca wine!

135
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:56,940
It contains cocaine!

136
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:57,740
It's a drug!

137
00:09:59,100 --> 00:09:59,780
Let go!

138
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:05,140
Move.

139
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:05,740
You promised me.

140
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:07,020
You have to take me there next time.

141
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:07,940
Then you'd better behave.

142
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,460
I always do what you say.

143
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:10,580
That's right.

144
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:14,300
Zhao.

145
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:16,100
Ding Yiyi.

146
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:17,780
What are you doing here?

147
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:20,340
I...

148
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:27,620
Come here.

149
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:30,820
Don't be afraid. I'm here.

150
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:31,980
Get your hands off her.

151
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:35,180
Ding Yiyi.

152
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:36,900
Come here and go home with me.

153
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:39,100
Mr. Ding.

154
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:42,500
There's no need to get angry.

155
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,220
Everyone comes to Kaimeili

156
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:45,780
to have a good time, don't they?

157
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:46,940
What kind of good time?

158
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:47,740
Didn't you come here

159
00:10:47,740 --> 00:10:49,620
to have a good time with this lady too?

160
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:50,420
What?

161
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:51,540
You're allowed to have fun,

162
00:10:51,540 --> 00:10:52,620
but your sister isn't?

163
00:10:55,140 --> 00:10:56,220
Ding Yiyi, come here.

164
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:58,300
I brought Miss Mei here.

165
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:02,100
I'll take Miss Mei home.

166
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:03,460
Someone.

167
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:05,020
Take her to my car.

168
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:06,420
I brought Miss Mei here,

169
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:07,700
so I'm the one taking her home.

170
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:12,060
Who do you think you are?

171
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:20,660
How dare you fight over
a woman my nephew

172
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:21,580
has his eye on?

173
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:23,620
Take her away.

174
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:31,060
Mengde, don't.

175
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:31,820
He's my brother.

176
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:33,340
Zhao!

177
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:36,060
Uncle Mengde.

178
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:43,100
Miss Mei!

179
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:48,620
Are you all right?

180
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:52,820
Are you both all right?

181
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:54,420
Mr. Jing.

182
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:55,980
I couldn't see clearly in the rain.

183
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:57,020
I almost ran you two over.

184
00:11:57,060 --> 00:11:58,020
I'm terribly sorry.

185
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,340
Go on, keep running.

186
00:12:01,340 --> 00:12:02,420
Mengde!

187
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:05,100
Boss Lv.

188
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:09,780
Mr. Jing.

189
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:15,220
Sorry if my guest frightened you.

190
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:15,940
My apologies.

191
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:16,720
What's this about?

192
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:20,900
There's been a misunderstanding
with Mr. Ding.

193
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:21,740
We'll settle it right away.

194
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:22,220
Someone!

195
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:23,140
Take them inside.

196
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:24,500
Instead of dealing
with these misunderstandings,

197
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:26,500
shouldn't you go home
and handle your family affairs?

198
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:28,500
What do you mean?

199
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:30,500
Mr. Kuang has arrived in Shanghai.

200
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:31,620
He's at the Kun Society now,

201
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:33,940
discussing Mr. Dong's funeral
arrangements with my adoptive father.

202
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:35,140
Why waste

203
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:36,620
your valuable time on these people?

204
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:40,180
Mengde.

205
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:44,420
Be good. Wait to hear from me.

206
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:53,780
Well?

207
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:55,420
Given up now?

208
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:58,660
Come home with me.

209
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:00,380
Let's go.

210
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:02,540
It seems you have family matters
to handle too, Mr. Ding.

211
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:04,020
If you trust me,

212
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:06,220
I can take this young lady
to the hospital first.

213
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:13,220
That won't be necessary.

214
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:15,820
In that case,

215
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:17,140
Jiusheng,

216
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:18,820
drive them home.

217
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:20,100
Thank you.

218
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:27,340
Father.

219
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:29,140
You're back.

220
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:30,560
Hmm.

221
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:51,780
Are you certain he died
at his mistress's hands?

222
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:57,980
Where is she?

223
00:13:58,140 --> 00:13:59,420
She's being held in the basement,

224
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:00,900
awaiting your return
to decide what to do with her.

225
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:05,300
On my way back,

226
00:14:05,660 --> 00:14:06,820
I stopped by the Kun Society.

227
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:09,020
I've already discussed it with Boss Ren.

228
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:12,220
In a few days, we'll hold

229
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:14,940
a farewell banquet
at home with the Kun Society

230
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:16,420
to bring this matter

231
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:18,820
to a close in the public's eyes.

232
00:14:19,340 --> 00:14:20,180
A farewell banquet?

233
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:22,540
You don't think
we've been humiliated enough?

234
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:23,860
You want to invite people over
to laugh at us,

235
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:24,420
is that it?

236
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:25,940
Since they want something
to laugh about,

237
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:27,220
we should present ourselves with dignity

238
00:14:27,420 --> 00:14:29,020
and give them nothing to laugh at.

239
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:29,620
Father.

240
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:30,380
Enough.

241
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,220
I've made up my mind.

242
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:33,820
You needn't concern yourself with this.

243
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:08,820
I must have frightened you tonight.

244
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,420
Uncle Mengde.

245
00:15:12,660 --> 00:15:13,460
I'm sorry.

246
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:15,340
I caused you trouble.

247
00:15:17,340 --> 00:15:18,580
I really didn't expect this.

248
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:20,860
All I did was offer Miss Mei

249
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,780
a glass of our signature wine.

250
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:25,220
How did she end up like that?

251
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:27,020
I ruined your plans.

252
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:28,860
Could it be

253
00:15:29,820 --> 00:15:31,060
there was something in the wine?

254
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:39,620
She simply couldn't handle her alcohol.

255
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:40,980
Yijie.

256
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:43,100
Next time you take a liking to someone,

257
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:44,460
don't be so impulsive.

258
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:45,820
Don't just offer her a drink like that.

259
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:47,660
It's not gentlemanly.

260
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:49,620
Girls won't appreciate it.

261
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,420
Sorry for the trouble,

262
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:52,500
Uncle Mengde.

263
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:56,380
It's nothing serious.

264
00:15:57,180 --> 00:15:58,260
It was only a glass of wine.

265
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:00,860
Yijie.

266
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:02,900
Whatever kind of girl
you like in the future,

267
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:04,420
just tell me.

268
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:05,740
I'll introduce you to someone.

269
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:09,780
Thank you, Uncle Mengde.

270
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:12,540
Good boy.

271
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:14,340
Come visit me more often.

272
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:20,400
♪And watch the lights
come on one by one♪

273
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:23,800
♪Like blades cutting
through the radiance♪

274
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:27,280
♪You may treat me as dust
beneath your feet♪

275
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:29,200
♪Or wipe me away like ashes♪

276
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,760
♪Leaving a cold ending♪

277
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:32,720
♪But I refuse to fall♪

278
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:37,630
♪I refuse to become a shadow
fading beneath the lights♪

279
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:40,190
♪I refuse to dissolve into♪

280
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:44,280
♪The lifeless light of the past♪

281
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:47,440
♪I want sharpness at my fingertips♪

282
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:50,280
♪And steps that avoid
the traps among the thorns♪

283
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:53,880
♪At dawn, I will look
straight into your eyes♪

284
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:57,080
♪My gaze clear, illuminating the dawn♪

285
00:16:58,550 --> 00:17:01,320
♪Those who have hurt me♪

286
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:04,560
♪I choose to pierce through♪

287
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:07,640
♪To tear apart♪

288
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:13,620
♪To ignite a sacred flame♪

289
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,440
♪I do not pray to the gods♪

290
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:20,370
♪Nor bow to power♪

291
00:17:20,370 --> 00:17:22,630
♪I will no longer play the tragic lead♪

292
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:28,340
♪I will stand and carve
the path of my own fate♪
